> If you've read Dante's Inferno, you'll know why I think Hell should be
> only 9 levels of mazes, each maze becoming smaller in area size and
> with walls impossible to dig into or teleport around.

Hey, I was thinking the same thing... it /would/ be cool (!) to
use Dante's Inferno as a model for (part of) Hell.

The different levels ("bowges") could each have characteristic monsters,
maybe even monsters representative of the sins associated with the level.
And they could have geographical characteristics representative of levels
of the Inferno, too...  I can't think of good examples right now... it's
been too long since I read the Inferno...  but I'm thinking of people
running around in circles, mud, people eating themselves...

