Actually, I think it would be more in character for Lucifer to betray
the player...  E.g., if you bring the amulet to him, he puts it on,
and then "grants you the gift of immortality" -- but then he seizes you
in his jaws and gnaws on you for eternity.  (Along with Judas Iscariot
and Brutus.)  In other words you could not die, but you could not win
the game; your only option would be to quit.  What greater punishment
could there be?

